**Assignment** Visual Prompt Studio 1.1: The Sci-Fi Film Poster Challenge
**Prompt** The poster shows a restrainted draconic creature with a menacing mansion in the background that has a eerie coloration and feel. Many forms of linees are present in this peice but the most direct is the fence line used as a bottom for the peice and the organic lines and in-organic (chains) lines used to draw attendion to the main attraction, the dracion creature. The peice is dominanted by many squares, triangles, and rectrangles, in such a way that gives the piece a very sinister and spooky look. As for texture it is apperently obvisous the draconic creature has a few different texture on it to aid in the apperence of an oraganic look, the building in the background has a more reduced and midevil looking feel. the contrast of the mansions greens and the dragons, whites and purples give a nice contrast to the otherwise dark feeling of the piece. 
**Vocabulary Breakdown** Lines - Lines are used to direct the views eyes towards a focal point in the piece or show contrast ment to invoke thought. Shapes - Shapes are used to convey emotions, patterns, overall harmony and balance of an art peice. Textures - A Texture is used to show the perceived feeling on an object, such as smooth or cracked, rough or bumpy. Volume - Volume is used to exagerate and minimize things within an art peice to gain or diverte attention, larger volumes of light will likely catch a viewers eye better than dull shadows. Contrast - contrast is a difference in the hue or opacity of a peice, contrasting and compilmentary colors are normally the preffered mean of showing this off, but shadows and highlights are just as effective. 
